## Limitations

- The corpus is small and domain-narrow; results may not transfer to other document types.
- The golden set is hand-written and limited in size, so metric differences between close configurations may be noise.
- Table and figure understanding is limited to what the parser extracts.
- Tenant isolation is enforced at the application and vector-store filter level, not at the infrastructure level.
- Single-node deployment; no horizontal scaling.

## Future work

- Entity graph / GraphRAG for multi-hop questions, compared against the baseline
- Feedback loop: user ratings feed new golden cases, with case-based memory for similar past queries
- Multimodal figure and table question answering with a vision-language model
- Fine-tuned reranker or embedding model using synthetic hard negatives
- Semantic caching with measured hit rate and cost savings
- Load testing (Locust) and a latency/cost dashboard
- Prompt-injection defenses for malicious text inside uploaded PDFs
- MCP server exposing the service as a tool
- A/B framework for chunking strategies
